--z3-tactic is the default tactic of the solver of the verdict only. An
auxiliary check (here --eq-audit, which runs without a verdict under
--vcgen-only) keeps z3's own: a tactic z3 rejects would make its checks
unknown if it reached them (it did, when the tactic was a global parameter).
RUN: sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --eq-audit --vcgen-only --z3-tactic=nosuchtactic 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=AUX
AUX: eq-audit: source=row-memop items=1 sampled=1 L0=0 L1=0 L2=1 undecided=0 unknown=0
The verdict solver gets it (and reports a tactic z3 rejects):
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-tactic=nosuchtactic 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VERDICT
VERDICT: Error: z3 rejects --z3-tactic 'nosuchtactic': {{.*}} [vc.z3-tactic]
RUN: sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-tactic=smtfd 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAT
SAT: solver.z3-tactic: smtfd
SAT: result: sat

